1. Nf3 d5 2. d4 Nf6 3. c4 e6 4. g3 dxc4 5. Bg2 c5  (5... Nc6  6. Qa4! {[%csl Gb4][%cal Ga4e8,Ge1h1,Gb1a3,Gc1d2,Gf8b4]if nc6 white should pin the knight and try to win back the c pawn. often nh6 is an idea. } Bb4+  (6... Bd7  7. Qxc4 Bb4+ 8. Nc3) 7. Bd2 Nd5 8. Bxb4 Nxb4 9. O-O Rb8 {[%cal Gb1a3]} 10. Na3)  (5... Bb4+ {simply block with the bishop, forcing them to respond straight away. }  6. Bd2 Bxd2+  (6... a5  7. Qc1 {[%cal Gb4d2,Gb1d2]immediately targetting the c4 pawn. Qc1 is better than Qc2 because it targets the dark squares on the kingside which may be weak if black decides to trade the bishops} c5 8. a3)  (6... c5  7. a3 Bxd2+ 8. Nbxd2 cxd4 9. Nxc4) 7. Qxd2! {[%cal Gb1a3,Ga3c4]activating the queen and looking at the dark squares on the kingside. White shouldn't be too scared of ne4 becausue firstly it walks into the bishop's xray and secondly the queen to go to f4 where it is very well placed and un challenged by a dark square bishop that black just traded} Bd7 {[%cal Gd2g5,Gb1a3]}  (7... O-O  8. Na3 Nc6 9. Nxc4) 8. Ne5 Bc6 9. Nxc6 Nxc6 10. Na3 Qd7 11. e3) 6. O-O Nc6  (6... cxd4  ) 7. dxc5! {in my game against reginald mba I went Qa4 which is not the best. When they go c5 in general in the catalan, normally the best move is to just take c5. The enndgame is still practically very favourable because of my light squared bishop which gets more powerful as lines open up} Qxd1 8. Rxd1 Bxc5 {[%cal Gb1d2,Gd2c4]} 9. Nbd2 b5?! {black's light squared bishop is a serious problem. If they ever  move the b pawn then ne5 ideas hang in the air. but at the same time developing to d7 is passive. }  (9... Ng4  10. Ne4)  (9... c3  10. bxc3 O-O {[%cal Gf3e1,Ge1d3]} 11. Bb2 Bd7 12. Nb3 Be7 13. c4) 10. Ne5! Nxe5 11. Bxa8 Ke7 12. Ne4 *

